    [Doc] Align PCP and DCP support documentation (#18736)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Update context-parallel documentation to reflect MRV2 PCP support and
    current feature combinations. Add PCP to the feature matrix, correct PCP
    compatibility with PP, DP and multimodal inputs, and include SFA
    speculative decoding support.
    
    Separate standalone DCP constraints from PCP+DCP topologies: MLA/SFA
    support DCP=PCP or TP*PCP, while GQA supports DCP=PCP. Align the DCP
    backend/hardware table and clarify replicated-indexer selection, SFA
    interleave sizing and the DSA-CP MRV1 requirement.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No runtime or API changes; documentation only.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Markdownlint, codespell and typos passed for all four changed
    documents.
    - Checked Markdown table widths, local link targets, footnote references
    and `git diff --check`.
    - Cross-checked existing PCP+DP, PCP+PP+MTP and PCP+DCP+MTP
    configurations and implementation paths; NPU tests were not rerun for
    this documentation-only change.
    - Attempted `bash format.sh ci`; full lint could not complete because
    the actionlint Go environment download timed out.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c4df37dfcc7f72ca41cd43801a468526ecf99a2b
    
